{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"title":"Events","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Events","modules":[{"name":"Events"}],"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The types every other module shares: the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/events"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event is a value that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", declared with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":". Its stored properties","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are its properties, so a misspelled or mistyped one is a compile error. Its type gives the name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations record it under, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" whose consent decides whether it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered, and the version of its shape. Each has a default: the type’s name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two property types carry rules of their own. A "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value, such as an email address,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prints as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<redacted>"},{"type":"text","text":" and has no public accessor: a destination reads it through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord\/reveal(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" once a delivery has redacted the record. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value satisfies every "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refinement"},{"type":"text","text":" lists, checked once as it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made: its initializer throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/UnsatisfiedConstraint"},{"type":"text","text":" for a value that breaks one. Each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling throws "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/InvalidConstraint"},{"type":"text","text":" for an argument no schema can hold, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a negative length."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker (module "},{"code":"Trackers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") makes an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of each event it tracks: the event, its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random identifier, when and where it was tracked, and the "},{"code":"ServiceContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" it was tracked in."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Destinations receive batches of these records. An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Enricher","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" adds to a record’s context: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker runs it on every record, or a destination’s "},{"code":"enriched(by:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the records it receives."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare an event with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":", part of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":"). It derives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" conformance from the struct’s declaration and fills in its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":" beside a property fills in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event\/constraintViolation()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". To write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance by hand instead, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Traffluent","","enum PlanName: Refinement {","    stati